   "source": [
    "**MPNN2 ≈ MPNN4 — the *type* of bounded normalization doesn't matter, only the bounding.**\n",
    "MPNN2 and MPNN4 use the **same 200** RDKit-2D descriptors, differing only in how they're normalized:\n",
    "MPNN2 via descriptastorus's **parametric** CDF (`rdkit_2d_normalized`), MPNN4 via an **empirical**\n",
    "`QuantileTransformer` on the raw values. Their held-out Pearson r is near-identical (Δ ≤ 0.013, MPNN2\n",
    "marginally ahead on 3/4 endpoints — within run-to-run noise). So what helps a neural net is squashing the\n",
    "descriptors into a **bounded [0, 1]** range; whether the CDF is fitted parametrically or empirically is a\n",
    "wash. This is the result that lets **FCNN2** (§ TBD) safely reuse either normalization rather than\n",
    "re-deriving the choice — see the scaling-choice inspection in `01.5` §4.1a for why bounding matters at all.\n"
   ]
  },
